"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[5545],{527926:e=>{e.exports="# ETL Pipeline Modernization\n\nSQL Agent jobs and batch pipeline patterns → Databricks Workflows and Delta Live Tables.\n\n> This doc is dialect-agnostic — pipeline structure is the same regardless of source dialect. Source dialect differences only affect the individual SQL steps inside each task, which are covered by the other reference files.\n\n## Output format guidance\n\nChoose the output format based on the source artifact and the user's target:\n\n| Source                                | Recommended output                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| T-SQL statements / stored procedures  | DBSQL code blocks (the normal migration output)                                       |\n| SQL Agent job (multi-step, scheduled) | A prose mapping of job steps → Workflow tasks, plus converted SQL for each T-SQL step |\n\nIf the user has not specified their target (Workflows vs DLT), ask before producing output — the two paths produce very different artifacts.\n\n## SQL Server Agent Jobs → Databricks Workflows\n\nSQL Agent jobs are scheduled multi-step jobs where each step is a T-SQL script or command.\n\n**Migration approach:**\n\n1. Map each job step → a Databricks Workflow task\n2. Steps with T-SQL → Databricks SQL task or Notebook task\n3. Job schedule → Workflow trigger (cron)\n\n```\nSQL Agent Job          → Databricks Workflow\n├── Step 1 (T-SQL)    → SQL task: truncate + load staging\n├── Step 2 (T-SQL)    → SQL task: run transformation query\n└── Step 3 (T-SQL)    → SQL task: archive and notify\n```\n\n## Batch ETL pattern\n\n**Watermark table** — tracks the last-processed timestamp so each run only processes new rows. Create it once before the first pipeline run:\n\n```sql\n-- Create the watermark table once\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS my_catalog.staging.watermark (\n    table_name STRING,\n    last_updated_at TIMESTAMP\n);\nINSERT INTO my_catalog.staging.watermark VALUES ('orders', TIMESTAMP '1970-01-01 00:00:00');\n```\n\n**Incremental load + MERGE** — the standard pattern for each pipeline run:\n\n```sql\n-- Use Unity Catalog three-part names: catalog.schema.table\nTRUNCATE TABLE my_catalog.staging.orders;\n\nINSERT INTO my_catalog.staging.orders\nSELECT * FROM source_catalog.source_schema.orders\nWHERE updated_at > (SELECT last_updated_at FROM my_catalog.staging.watermark WHERE table_name = 'orders');\n\nMERGE INTO my_catalog.target_schema.orders t\nUSING my_catalog.staging.orders s ON t.order_id = s.order_id\nWHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *\nWHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;\n\n-- Advance the watermark after a successful merge\nUPDATE my_catalog.staging.watermark\nSET last_updated_at = (SELECT MAX(updated_at) FROM my_catalog.staging.orders)\nWHERE table_name = 'orders';\n```\n"}}]);
